# Nx libs & boundaries

Every app/lib is tagged in `project.json`, enforced by
`@nx/enforce-module-boundaries` in `eslint.config.mjs`:

- `scope:customer` / `scope:staff` / `scope:api` — apps can only depend on
  their own scope plus `scope:shared`.
- `scope:shared` — libs usable from any app (`libs/frontend/ui`,
  `libs/frontend/auth-client`, `libs/shared/util`).
- `type:ui` — UI-only libs can only depend on other `type:ui`/`type:util` libs.

When adding a new shared frontend lib: generate it under
`libs/frontend/<name>` (e.g. `npx nx g @nx/angular:library ...`), tag it
`["scope:shared", "type:<ui|util|data-access>"]`, and confirm its path landed
in `tsconfig.base.json` (the generator does this automatically).

Backend feature modules live in `libs/backend/<name>` and are wired into
`apps/api` via `@restaurant-os/<name>`.
